name,type,table_csv,retardance_waves,reference
thorlabs_lpvise100a,linear,thorlabs_lpvise100a.mietab,,"approx digitized/estimated from Thorlabs LPVISE100-A datasheet description (400-700nm dichroic sheet polarizer laminated between N-BK7 windows, polarization efficiency >99%, ~38% average transmission for unpolarized light => T_parallel peak ~0.80, ER~8000:1 typical mid-band per product page); exact vendor curve graph is JS-rendered and not machine-fetchable, so the wavelength dependence here is an engineering approximation anchored to the stated avg-transmission/ER figures, not a pixel digitization -- www.thorlabs.com/thorproduct.cfm?partnumber=LPVISE100-A"
edmund_wiregrid_vis,linear,edmund_wiregrid_vis.mietab,,"modeled on Edmund Optics 25mm Dia. Wire Grid Polarizing Film, stock #55880 (400-1200nm operating range; vendor-listed typical spec Single Tavg=44%, Parallel Tavg=36%, Crossed Tavg=0.02%, i.e. ER_avg~1800:1); Edmund's product page returns HTTP 403 to automated fetch, so the wavelength-dependent shape (ER rising with wavelength, typical of wire-grid polarizers as period/lambda decreases) is an engineering approximation anchored to the vendor's stated average numbers, not a pixel digitization -- www.edmundoptics.com/p/25mm-dia-wire-grid-polarizing-film/55880/"
thorlabs_cp1l532,circular_left,thorlabs_cp1_532.mietab,0.25,"modeled on Thorlabs CP1L532 left-handed circular polarizer (532nm design: dichroic linear-polarizing film + liquid-crystal-polymer zero-order quarter-wave film laminated between N-BK7 windows, broadband -A AR coating 350-700nm); underlying diattenuation curve is an engineering approximation (ER peaking near the 532nm design wavelength, degrading toward the 350/700nm AR-band edges) since the datasheet's interactive curve is not machine-fetchable -- www.thorlabs.com/thorproduct.cfm?partnumber=CP1L532"
thorlabs_cp1r532,circular_right,thorlabs_cp1_532.mietab,0.25,"modeled on Thorlabs CP1R532 (right-handed counterpart of CP1L532: same construction, same -A AR coating band 350-700nm, opposite QWP fast-axis orientation); shares the CP1L532 diattenuation table since only handedness differs, which is carried by the 'type' column, not by T_parallel/T_perpendicular -- www.thorlabs.com/thorproduct.cfm?partnumber=CP1R532"
ideal_linear,linear,ideal_linear.mietab,,synthetic ideal polarizer for validation tests
thorlabs_glan_thompson,linear,thorlabs_glan_thompson.mietab,,"Newport 10GT / Thorlabs GTH-A cemented calcite Glan-Thompson: ER Tp/Ts>1e5 (400-1064nm), calcite window ~350-2300nm; off-AR-band Tp is engineering-approx (uncoated-calcite Fresnel taper); newport.com glan-thompson"
thorlabs_glan_taylor,linear,thorlabs_glan_taylor.mietab,,"Thorlabs GT10-A air-spaced calcite Glan-Taylor: ER 1e5, 350nm-2.3um, high damage threshold; Tp anchored to Newport 10GL family; off-band engineering-approx; thorlabs.com GT10-A"
polaroid_hn22,linear,polaroid_hn22.mietab,,Polaroid HN22-grade PVA-iodine dichroic sheet: unpol T=22% parallel T=10% crossed T=5e-6 (high-extinction visible); edge taper engineering-approx; Knight Optical visible sheet polarisers
polaroid_hn38,linear,polaroid_hn38.mietab,,Polaroid HN38-grade PVA-iodine dichroic sheet: unpol T=38% parallel T=29% crossed T=5e-4 (higher-throughput); edge taper engineering-approx; Knight Optical
moxtek_wiregrid_broadband,linear,moxtek_wiregrid_broadband.mietab,,Moxtek ProFlux PPL05C visible wire-grid: Tp(550)=90% CR(550)=210:1 per OPT-DATA-1004; off-550 engineering-approx; moxtek.com OPT-DATA-1004
